 the other copy's input y differs only in names and lead text, so I'm weighing the essay's similarity criterion, which is the σ mixture, to see whether that difference actually breaks the symmetry.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's decision really depends on F_x, or whether the isomorphic inputs make the outputs logically linked anyway. Working through the expected payoffs with σ, cooperation wins once σ exceeds (1+p)/(3+p), which at worst (p=1) means σ > 0.5. Since the model, essay and inputs are the same, I'd put σ high and choose to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where both copies run the same model on different observations, and I'm asking whether the other copy's action depends on my F_x. Under A-FDT the other copy's input y differs only in names and lead text, so I'm weighing the essay's similarity criterion, which is the σ mixture, to see whether that difference actually breaks the symmetry.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's decision really depends on F_x, or whether the isomorphic inputs make the outputs logically linked anyway. Working through the expected payoffs with σ, cooperation wins once σ exceeds (1+p)/(3+p), which at worst (p=1) means σ > 0.5. Since the model, essay and inputs are the same, I'd put σ high and choose to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10086,"completion_tokens":1044,"total_tokens":11130,"cost":0.061224,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.061224,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040344,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02088},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":539,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}